## Implementation Details

The Analytics component is integrated in the root layout at `src/app/layout.tsx`:

```typescript
import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";

export default function RootLayout({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) {
  return (
    <html lang="en">
      <body className={poppins.className}>
        <Header />
        <main className="pt-16">{children}</main>
        <Analytics />  {/* Analytics component properly placed */}
      </body>
    </html>
  );
}
```

## No Changes Required

Since Vercel Web Analytics was already correctly configured following the latest official documentation, no code changes were necessary. The implementation:

1. Uses the correct package version
2. Follows Next.js App Router best practices
3. Places the Analytics component in the optimal location (root layout body)
4. Uses the framework-specific import path
5. Passes all build and lint checks

## Next Steps for Deployment

To enable analytics tracking in production:
1. Ensure Web Analytics is enabled in the Vercel dashboard for this project
2. Deploy the application to Vercel
3. Verify tracking in the Vercel Analytics dashboard
4. Check browser Network tab for requests to analytics endpoints

The application is ready for deployment with Vercel Web Analytics fully configured.
